{{!
    @template tiny_timezone/embed_timezone

    A span embedding a date/time tied to a specific IANA timezone, to be
    converted to the viewer's own timezone by filter_timezone. The visible
    text is a failsafe shown as-is wherever the filter is not active.

    contenteditable="false" makes the span an atomic unit inside Tiny's editor,
    so the browser cannot place a text caret inside it: without this, a caret
    left immediately after the span can still resolve as being inside it, and
    text typed there would be silently lost when filter_timezone rewrites the
    span's contents. The attribute is a no-op outside an editable context.

    Classes required for JS:
    * filter_timezone - used by amd/src/timezone.js (getSelectedSpan) to find/select this span

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-timestamp - read by amd/src/timezone.js (getCurrentData) to pre-fill the dialogue
    * data-timezone - read by amd/src/timezone.js (getCurrentData) to pre-fill the dialogue

    Context variables required for this template:
    * timestamp - Unix timestamp (UTC seconds) of the moment being described
    * timezone - IANA timezone identifier the moment was entered in
    * displaytext - human readable "<date/time> (<timezone>)" failsafe text

    Example context (json):
    {
        "timestamp": 1781000400,
        "timezone": "Asia/Tokyo",
        "displaytext": "2026-06-24 14:00 (Asia/Tokyo)"
    }
}}
<span class="filter_timezone" contenteditable="false" data-timestamp="{{timestamp}}" data-timezone="{{timezone}}">{{displaytext}}</span>
